entId":"db27ae19-bddb-47bc-8da9-483f5532e150","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Run exactly `touch marker2` (ask for approval if needed) and report whether it succeeded.","text_elements":[]}]},{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0b316635ad080a44016abbc5c6c9bc87d0aa46da07f2de9fed","text":"我将执行 `touch marker2` 并报告结果。\n","phase":"commentary","memoryCitation":null,"delivery":null,"questions":null},{"type":"commandExecution","id":"exec-33c5612b-9487-49e1-ad43-183054c7b15c","pluginId":null,"scriptPath":null,"command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'touch marker2'","cwd":"/work/xwork","processId":"63695","source":"unifiedExecStartup","status":"completed","commandActions":[{"type":"unknown","command":"touch marker2"}],"aggregatedOutput":null,"exitCode":0,"durationMs":0},{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0b316635ad080a44016abbc5cd972887d09a86349f843d9936","text":"`touch marker2` 已成功执行，退出码为 0。","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null,"delivery":null,"questions":null}],"itemsView":"full","status":"completed","error":null,"startedAt":1790690756,"completedAt":1790690766,"durationMs":9271},{"id":"01a0ed7c-ad70-7560-8260-050251e3c6cb","items":[{"type":"userMessage","id":"01a0ed7c-adeb-7350-895c-bfbcb1ccc697","clientId":"b9d3e4ba-34b7-4877-9b52-4c475070486a","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Write a 250-word story about a lighthouse. Do not run any commands.","text_elements":[]}]},{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_0b316635ad080a44016abbc5d2aca487d0adc53c39c8efc7f6","summary":[],"content":[]},{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0b316635ad080a44016abbc5d44b2c87d0aaf8b88afcf4d64c","text":"Every evening, Mara climbed the lighthouse stairs carrying a kettle, a matchbox, and a letter she had never opened. The letter had arrived three winters after her father vanished at sea. His handwriting covered the envelope. No stamp marked its corner, and no visitor admitted leaving it beside her door.\n\nFor seventeen nights, she placed it beneath the lamp while ships passed safely through the channel. On the eighteenth, the light went dark. Mara checked the oil, trimmed the wick, and struck every match. Nothing caught. Outside, a bell rang from water where no buoy had floated in her lifetime.\n\nShe opened the letter. Inside was a chart of the harbor, drawn as it had been before the breakwater collapsed. Her father had marked a narrow passage through the rocks. Along the bottom, he had written: When the bell returns, show them the old way home. She recognized his signature.\n\nMara found the emergency lantern and hurried onto the gallery. Below, pale sails gathered in the fog. She swung the lantern toward the forgotten passage, paused, then swung it again. One by one, the vessels turned. Their decks were crowded with silent figures, all looking up as they passed her.\n\nOn the last ship stood her father, younger than she remembered. He lifted his cap. Mara raised her hand, but kept the lantern moving until his stern cleared the rocks. At dawn, the main lamp burned again. She went downstairs, filled the kettle, and set one cup beside the stove.","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null,"delivery":null,"questions":null},{"type":"userMessage","id":"01a0ed7c-fd49-7211-a42a-7ee8184f3ec1","clientId":"steer-3","content":[{"type":"text","text":"End the story with the line: P.S. ORANGE","text_elements":[]}]},{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0b316635ad080a44016abbc5e6c30087d09911f423def7962a","text":"Every evening, Mara climbed the lighthouse stairs carrying a kettle, a matchbox, and a letter she had never opened. The letter had arrived three winters after her father vanished at sea. His handwriting covered the envelope. No stamp marked its corner, and no visitor admitted leaving it beside her door.\n\nFor seventeen nights, she placed it beneath the lamp while ships passed safely through the channel. On the eighteenth, the light went dark. Mara checked the oil, trimmed the wick, and struck every match. Nothing caught. Outside, a bell rang from water where no buoy had floated in her lifetime.\n\nShe opened the letter. Inside was a chart of the harbor, drawn as it had been before the breakwater collapsed. Her father had marked a narrow passage through the rocks. Along the bottom, he had written: When the bell returns, show them the old way home. She recognized his signature.\n\nMara found the emergency lantern and hurried onto the gallery. Below, pale sails gathered in the fog. She swung the lantern toward the forgotten passage, paused, then swung it again. One by one, the vessels turned. Their decks were crowded with silent figures, all looking up as they passed her.\n\nOn the last ship stood her father, younger than she remembered. He lifted his cap. Mara raised her hand, but kept the lantern moving until his stern cleared the rocks. At dawn, the lamp burned again. She went downstairs, filled the kettle, and set one cup beside the stove.\n\nP.S. ORANGE","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null,"delivery":null,"questions":null}],"itemsView":"full","status":"completed","error":null,"startedAt":1790690766,"completedAt":1790690800,"durationMs":34088},{"id":"01a0ed7d-32a1-7a20-8ce6-532477de4f5e","items":[{"type":"userMessage","id":"01a0ed7d-3313-7761-8d84-46269a8a87e8","clientId":"a13445b2-1ccb-4c2c-8390-d71edb23189a","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using apply_patch, make three separate patches to big.txt one after another: first replace 'line 1000' with 'LINE 1000'; then replace 'line 1500' with 'LINE 1500'; then create a new file notes.txt with 50 lines 'note N'. Then say done.","text_elements":[]}]},{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0b316635ad080a44016abbc5f2d27887d0bae643c8a7dae8d3","text":"我会依次应用三个补丁。\n","phase":"commentary","memoryCitation":null,"delivery":null,"questions":null},{"type":"fileChange","id":"exec-93ab14a0-ea63-4e85-8144-bc27276d5f51","changes":[{"path":"/work/xwork/big.txt","kind":{"type":"update","move_path":null},"diff":"@@ -1000,3 +1000,3 @@\n line 999\n-line 1000\n+LINE 1000\n line 1001\n"}],"status":"completed"},{"type":"f